>> title: Cơm Tấm
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: pork, rice, vietnamese, lemongrass, grill
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: com tam, cơm tấm, cơm tấm sườn nướng, com tam suon nuong, broken rice, broken rice plate, grilled pork chop with rice, rice plate, C1
>> pairs-with: nuoc-cham, do-chua
>> servings: 4
>> time: 4 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the marinade is mostly sugar, so the chop lacquers and then blackens inside the same ten minutes over the fire

>> step: stir the marinade
Stir @lemongrass{2%stalks}(minced fine), @garlic{3%cloves}(minced), @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), @fish sauce{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @dark soy sauce{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @white pepper{1/2%tsp} and @vegetable oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) into a marinade.

>> step: marinate chilled 4 hr
Marinate @bone-in pork chops{4}(1/2 inch thick, pounded thinner and scored through the fat) in @&(~1)marinade{} in the #fridge{} ~marinate{4%hr}.

>> step: rinse, steam 20 min, rest 10 min
Rinse @broken rice{2%cup}(370 g) until the water runs nearly clear, then steam it with @water{2 1/4%cup}(535 mL) ~steam{20%min} and ~rest{10%min} off the heat with the lid on.

>> step: grill 10 min, basting
Grill @&(~2)pork chops{} over hot coals ~grill{10%min}, turning and basting with what is left in the dish, until the edges blacken and the fat crisps.

>> step: top the rice, dress the plate
Top @&(~2)broken rice{} with @&(~1)grilled chop{} laid over it, spoon @scallion oil{2%Tbs} across the rice, and set @đồ chua{1/2%cup}(drained), @cucumber{1/2}(sliced) and @tomato{1}(sliced) alongside with @nước chấm{1/2%cup} to pour over the whole plate at once.
